    "question": {
      ":question/id": "785a58d5-601a-50af-b1f2-100d273d37ef",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{2}{64 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the linear substitution $u=8 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=8,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{8})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{2}{64 x^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 2\\int \\frac{1}{1+(8 x)^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 2(\\frac{1}{8})\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{1+u^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(u \\right)}}{4}+C \\\\  &= \\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(8 x \\right)}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
